\merge draws two or more instruments on the staff of the
first one, as voices, like LilyPond does.
Its syntax is the following:

\merge \inst1 \inst2

The first instrument has its stems up, the second down, the
third up again, and so on. Merging changes only the score,
every instrument plays as before. The merged instruments
should have the same clef, as each voice is placed by its
own clef.

An instrument that is merged again leaves the staff it was
merged to before.

To draw instruments on their own staves again, use
\unmerge:

\unmerge \inst2

\merge takes at least two instruments. An unknown
instrument, or an instrument given more than once, throws
an error.
